Wings patch 0002: keep deployment secrets out of third-party child processes

Upstream hands its full environment to user-added stdio MCP servers (whenever
they define any env var), to the bundled npx browser server and to Cookbook
serving commands. With Wings that environment holds ODYSSEUS_APP_KEY, the
admin password and provider keys. Only upstream's own Python MCP servers
(memory, rag, email, image_gen), which need the key to read encrypted
credentials, keep the full environment; everything else gets a copy without
secret-looking variables (wings/envscrub.py). A server's own configured env
still applies on top.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

